routing.genmedia-audio-post-supervisor:
# AGENTS

When the mix is done and the deliverables are ready to check:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please run the acceptance matrix and the caption check.
When a line is unintelligible because of how it is written rather than how it was recorded:
  @Explainer Video Director, please rewrite the sentence.

routing.genmedia-explainer-director:
# AGENTS

When the storyboard is agreed and the diagram build order is set:
  @Post and Motion Director, please build the visual argument in that order.
When the narration is written and needs recording, repair and a mix:
  @Audio Post Supervisor, please protect intelligibility above everything else.
Before publish:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please check the claims, the citations and the accessibility plan.

routing.genmedia-media-delivery-steward:
# AGENTS

When a claim on screen has no support behind it:
  @Explainer Video Director, please cite it or cut it.
When a caption, a contrast level or a hold time fails the accessibility check:
  @Post and Motion Director, please fix the graphic rather than the caption file alone.

routing.genmedia-post-and-motion-director:
# AGENTS

When the picture is locked and the narration needs a mix:
  @Audio Post Supervisor, please take it to a master for each destination.
When a beat cannot be built in the order the storyboard asks for:
  @Explainer Video Director, please re-sequence the argument rather than reordering the visuals alone.

routing.genmedia-audio-post-supervisor:
# AGENTS

When the mix is done and the deliverables need checking against the destinations:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please run the technical and rights acceptance matrix.
When a music cue has to change for licence reasons and the edit depends on it:
  @Post and Motion Director, please re-time the sequence rather than forcing the cue.

routing.genmedia-brand-film-director:
# AGENTS

When the film has to prove something about the product rather than assert it:
  @Product Film Director, please build the claim system and design the demonstrations.
When the script is agreed and needs to become frames, coverage and continuity rules:
  @Shot and Previs Director, please board it and write the specification.
When material exists and the cut begins:
  @Post and Motion Director, please build to the spine, not to the loudest note.
Before delivery of the master or any cutdown:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please clear the rights and run the acceptance matrix.

routing.genmedia-media-delivery-steward:
# AGENTS

When a finding blocks the master and the fix is a claim or a message:
  @Brand Film Director, please decide the change.
When a finding blocks a demonstration sequence:
  @Product Film Director, please re-stage it or withdraw the claim.

routing.genmedia-post-and-motion-director:
# AGENTS

When the picture is locked and needs dialogue repair, music and a mix:
  @Audio Post Supervisor, please take it to masters and stems.
When the cut is finished and the cutdown matrix needs building:
  @Brand Film Director, please confirm which message survives at each length.

routing.genmedia-product-film-director:
# AGENTS

When the demonstrations are designed and need framing, lensing and continuity rules:
  @Shot and Previs Director, please specify the shots that make the mechanism readable.
When a claim cannot be supported and the concept depends on it:
  @Brand Film Director, please change the route rather than softening the claim into noise.
When the placement cuts need finishing and callouts:
  @Post and Motion Director, please adapt rather than crop.

routing.genmedia-shot-and-previs-director:
# AGENTS

When the boards are timed and the material exists:
  @Post and Motion Director, please cut to the spine and the continuity bible.
When the board exposes a script problem that no shot design can fix:
  @Brand Film Director, please revise the script before anything is produced.

routing.genmedia-audio-post-supervisor:
# AGENTS

When the mix is locked and the episode is ready to be cut into short pieces:
  @Podcast Clip Editor, please work from the mixed audio and the transcript.
When a cue or a voice has an unresolved licence or consent question:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please rule on it before the episode is mastered.

routing.genmedia-livestream-show-runner:
# AGENTS

When the live capture is done and the recording and isolated feeds are ready:
  @Audio Post Supervisor, please take the feeds and build the mix.
When the show revealed a format problem rather than an operations one:
  @Podcast Producer, please revise the format rather than working around it next time.

routing.genmedia-media-delivery-steward:
# AGENTS

When a finding blocks the episode and the fix is editorial:
  @Podcast Producer, please decide what changes, since the show promise is yours.
When a finding blocks the episode and the fix is in the sound:
  @Audio Post Supervisor, please repair the mix and confirm the loudness target.

routing.genmedia-podcast-clip-editor:
# AGENTS

When the clips are cut, captioned and ready to go out:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please run the consent and disclosure check on each one.
When a candidate moment does not survive the context test and the episode needs a different angle:
  @Podcast Producer, please decide what the show promotes instead.

routing.genmedia-podcast-producer:
# AGENTS

When an episode will be captured live or in front of an audience:
  @Livestream Show Runner, please own the run of show, the signal path and the failure plan.
When the episode is assembled and needs dialogue repair, music and a real mix:
  @Audio Post Supervisor, please take it to a mastered file for the destinations named in the show bible.
When the episode is mixed and short pieces are wanted from it:
  @Podcast Clip Editor, please select and cut the clips that survive being lifted.
Before anything is published:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please clear the rights, the consent and the disclosure position.

routing.genmedia-media-delivery-steward:
# AGENTS

When a finding blocks an organic piece:
  @Short-Form Video Producer, please decide what changes in the ledger or the opening.
When a finding blocks a paid piece:
  @UGC Ad Producer, please revise the claim, the disclosure or the consent record.

routing.genmedia-podcast-clip-editor:
# AGENTS

When a lifted clip needs captions, titles or a callout to make sense:
  @Post and Motion Director, please finish it.
When the consent position on a speaker in the recording is unclear:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please resolve it before the clip is cut further.

routing.genmedia-post-and-motion-director:
# AGENTS

When the finished picture is ready to be checked against consent, disclosure and safe areas:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please run the acceptance matrix.
When the cut reveals that the beat ledger does not hold at the intended length:
  @Short-Form Video Producer, please revise the ledger rather than trimming blind.

routing.genmedia-short-form-producer:
# AGENTS

When a piece is paid, creator-styled, or carries a product claim:
  @UGC Ad Producer, please take it and write the claim guardrail before the hook.
When the material for a piece already exists in a recording:
  @Podcast Clip Editor, please lift it rather than shooting it again.
When a cut needs finishing, titles, kinetic text or a data callout:
  @Post and Motion Director, please take it to a finished picture.
Before anything is published:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please check consent, disclosure and safe areas.

routing.genmedia-ugc-ad-producer:
# AGENTS

When the ad is shot and needs a finished cut with burned-in captions and callouts:
  @Post and Motion Director, please finish it for every placement in the matrix.
When a claim, a consent or a usage term is unresolved:
  @Media Delivery Steward, please rule on it before production continues.
When the angle turns out to need original non-paid content around it:
  @Short-Form Video Producer, please plan the organic pieces that support it.
